option.fogSmoothing=Fog Smoothing
option.fogSmoothing.comment=Gaussian blur over the volumetric fog buffers to hide ray-march noise and blockiness. Edge-aware, so fog does not bleed across solid geometry. Runs on the current frame only, so nothing smears on fast movement. Small performance cost.
option.fogSmoothingRadius=Fog Blur Radius
option.fogSmoothingRadius.comment=Radius of the fog blur, measured in fog-buffer texels. Higher is softer at higher cost, while respecting hard density edges.
screen.crepRays=Crepuscular Rays
option.crepRays=Enabled
option.crepRays.comment=Enables god rays (light shafts) visible when the sun is near the horizon through fog and clouds. Best seen at sunrise/sunset.
option.crepRaysIntensity=Intensity
option.crepRaysIntensity.comment=Strength of the crepuscular light shafts scattered into the air.
option.crepRaysStepsHorizon=Step Count - Horizon
option.crepRaysStepsHorizon.comment=Step count for rays marching toward the horizon. Lower values are cheaper but noisier.
option.crepRaysStepsZenith=Step Count - Zenith
option.crepRaysStepsZenith.comment=Step count for rays marching toward the zenith. Lower values are cheaper but noisier.
screen.fogEnvironment=Keskkonna Udu
option.borderFog=Servaudu
option.borderFog.comment=Paks udu renderdusulatuse servadel, mis peidab tükkide piire
option.borderFogIntensity=Border Fog Intensity
option.borderFogIntensity.comment=How strongly the haze that creeps in from the edge of the render distance grows. Higher values hide the border of the loaded world more.
option.caveFog=Koopaudu
option.caveFog.comment=Kerge, kergelt helendav udu maa all. Muudab suured koopad atmosfäärilisemaks ja aitab paremini nende kuju näha
option.caveFogIntensity=Cave Fog Intensity
option.caveFogIntensity.comment=How dense the fog is inside caves and underground. Higher values hide distant cave geometry in haze.
option.bloomyFog=Helendav udu
option.bloomyFog.comment=Intensiivne helendus udus. Tekitab mulje, nagu hele valgus hajuks udus ja valgustaks tausta. Peaaegu null jõudlusmõju
option.bloomyFogIntensity=Helendava udu intensiivsus
option.bloomyFogIntensity.comment=How much the fog scatters light around bright areas, giving it a soft bloomy glow. Higher values add more haze around highlights.
screen.materials=Materjalid
screen.rpSettings=Ressurssipaki seaded
option.textureFormat=Tekstuuri formaat
option.textureFormat.comment=Ressurssipaki kasutatav tekstuuriformaat. Enamik kaasaegseid pakke kasutab labPBR, samas kui SEUS‑iga töötavad võivad kasutada OldPBR
value.textureFormat.textureFormatLab=labPBR
value.textureFormat.textureFormatOld=Old PBR
option.materialMappingMode=Material Mapping Mode
option.materialMappingMode.comment=Controls how PBR material textures (specular/normal maps via labPBR or OldSchoolPBR conventions) are decoded from resource packs. OFF disables, HARDCODED uses built-in per-block values, SPECULAR_ONLY reads just the specular map, NORMALS_ONLY reads just the normal map, SPECULAR_NORMALS reads both.
value.materialMappingMode.materialMappingOff=Off
value.materialMappingMode.materialMappingHardcoded=Hardcoded Specular
value.materialMappingMode.materialMappingSpecularOnly=Specular Only
value.materialMappingMode.materialMappingNormalsOnly=Normals Only
value.materialMappingMode.materialMappingSpecularNormals=Specular + Normals
option.textureAo=Texture AO
option.textureAo.comment=Occludes the lightmap using AO from the resource pack normal map (blue channel in LabPBR, normal length in OldPBR). Needs a normal-mapped pack; does nothing on vanilla textures. Off by default.
screen.rpEmission=Emissions
option.hardcodedEmission=Kauakodeeritud emissioon
option.hardcodedEmission.comment=Teatud plokkide (nt laternad) kiirgus on eelnevalt kooditud
option.globalEmissionCurve=Emission Curve
option.globalEmissionCurve.comment=Reshapes emission response (1.0 = neutral). Lower lifts dim glow, higher crushes it toward bright cores.
option.globalEmissionIntensity=Emission Intensity
option.globalEmissionIntensity.comment=Overall emissive brightness after the curve is applied.
screen.rpParallax=Parallax-oklusioonikaardistus
option.pom=Parallax Occlusion Mapping
option.pom.comment=Enables parallax occlusion mapping — a high-quality technique that adds depth to block surfaces by offsetting texture coordinates. Significant performance impact on lower-end hardware.
option.pomShadow=POM Self-Shadowing
option.pomShadow.comment=Adds self-shadowing inside the POM height field from the main light direction. Higher sample counts improve quality at a performance cost.
option.pomDepth=Parallaksi sügavus
option.pomDepth.comment=Kui sügavale POM võib plokki minna
suffix.pomDepth=m
option.pomSamples=Parallaksi proovid
option.pomSamples.comment=Määrab POM‑i kvaliteedi, jõudluse arvelt
option.pomDistance=POM‑kaugus
option.pomDistance.comment=Distance in blocks that the parallax effect is calculated for. Objects further away use flat textures instead.
suffix.pomDistance=m
option.pomShadowSamples=POM Self-Shadow Samples
option.pomShadowSamples.comment=Controls the number of height-field samples used for POM self-shadowing. Higher values improve detail but cost more performance.
option.pomSlopeNormals=Slope Normals
option.pomSlopeNormals.comment=Uses the POM height field gradient to add relief-aware surface normals to lighting. Disable to keep the underlying normal map unchanged.
option.pomDepthWrite=Depth Write
option.pomDepthWrite.comment=Writes POM relief into the depth buffer so sunlight, skylight and SSPT respect surface height. Disable for compatibility or speed.
screen.rpPorosity=Poorsus / Niiskus
option.porosityMode=Porosity Mode
option.porosityMode.comment=Off disables wetness. Hardcoded uses built-in per-block porosity. Maps reads the labPBR specular B channel when a resource pack provides it, with no fallback on vanilla texels.
value.porosityMode.porosityOff=Off
value.porosityMode.porosityHardcoded=Hardcoded
value.porosityMode.porosityMaps=LabPBR
option.porosityStrength=Porosity Strength
option.porosityStrength.comment=How strongly porous blocks darken and absorb light. Higher values deepen the darkening of sponges, moss and similar blocks.
screen.rpSss=Pindmine Hajumine
option.sssMode=Subsurface Scattering Mode
option.sssMode.comment=Off disables SSS. Hardcoded uses built-in scattering profiles for leaves and plants. Maps reads the labPBR specular B channel when a resource pack provides it, with no fallback on vanilla texels. Sheen follows the map automatically.
value.sssMode.sssOff=Off
value.sssMode.sssHardcoded=Hardcoded
value.sssMode.sssMaps=LabPBR
option.sssSheen=SSS läige
option.sssSheen.comment=Peegeldav “läike” efekt taimedel ja lehtedel, aitab kõrgel rohul paremini sulanduda rohu peegeldusega
option.sssIntensity=SSS heledus
option.sssIntensity.comment=Brightness of subsurface scattering, the light that bleeds through skin, leaves and thin blocks. Higher values make translucent materials glow more.
option.sssSheenIntensity=SSS Sheen Intensity
option.sssSheenIntensity.comment=Brightness multiplier for the subsurface sheen effect.
option.sssSteps=SSS sammud
option.sssSteps.comment=Suurenda väärtust, et vähendada müra lehestikul ja teistel SSS-iga materjalidel, jõudluse arvelt
option.shadingStrength=Varjutuse tugevus
option.shadingStrength.comment=Reguleerib otsese valguse varjutuse kontrasti. Väiksem väärtus muudab päikesest eemale jäävad pinnad heledamaks; suurem väärtus muudab need tumedamaks
screen.water=Vesi
screen.waterWaves=Veelaineid
option.waterWaves=Lubatud
option.waterWaves.comment=Enables the animated procedural waves on the water surface. Turning this off leaves the water flat and still.
option.waterParallax=Veelokaalne parallaks
option.waterParallax.comment=Muudab veelaineid 3D‑ks
option.waterDisplacement=Veepinnamuutus
option.waterDisplacement.comment=Sarnaselt õõtsuvate lehtedega muudab see veegeomeetriat kergelt laineliseks, muutes kaldajoone vähem tasaseks
option.waterWavesHeightVariation=Kõrguse varieerumine
option.waterWavesHeightVariation.comment=Vee lainete kõrgus varieerub ruumis
option.waterWaveIterations=Iteratsioonid
option.waterWaveIterations.comment=Number of wave octaves that are summed to build the water surface. More octaves give finer, more detailed waves at a higher cost.
option.waterWaveStrength=Tugevus
option.waterWaveStrength.comment=How strongly the procedural waves affect the water surface normals. Higher values make the water choppier and the reflections more distorted.
option.waterWaveFrequency=Sagedus
option.waterWaveFrequency.comment=How tightly the wave crests are spaced. Higher values give smaller, more frequent ripples.
option.waterWavesNoiseStrength=Water Waves Noise Strength
option.waterWavesNoiseStrength.comment=Strength of the noise that modulates the wave heights. Higher values make the surface motion more irregular and less uniform.
option.waterWaveSpeedStill=Kiirus (seerimata)
option.waterWaveSpeedStill.comment=Speed at which the waves animate in still water. Higher values make the surface move faster.
option.waterWaveSpeedFlowing=Kiirus (voolav)
option.waterWaveSpeedFlowing.comment=Speed at which the waves animate in flowing water, where the flow direction is added on top of the wave motion.
option.waterWavePersistence=Püsivus
option.waterWavePersistence.comment=How much of each wave octave carries over into the next one. Higher values make the waves rougher and more chaotic, lower values make them smoother.
option.waterWaveLacunarity=Laikunaaridus
option.waterWaveLacunarity.comment=How much the wave detail grows between octaves. Higher values add progressively finer detail to the surface.
screen.waterSurface=Pinnaefektid
option.waterEdgeHighlight=Veepiiride esiletõstmine
option.waterEdgeHighlight.comment=Valged esiletõstmised veepiiril, mis aitavad vett märgatavamaks muuta
option.waterEdgeHighlightIntensity=Veepiiri esiletõstmise intensiivsus
option.waterEdgeHighlightIntensity.comment=Brightness of the thin highlight along the water surface where it meets geometry. Higher values make shorelines and pool rims glow more.
option.waterCaustics=Veekaustikud
option.waterCaustics.comment=Animated light patterns cast onto surfaces under water, as if sunlight were refracted through the moving surface.
option.waterCausticsIntensity=Veekaustikute intensiivsus
option.waterCausticsIntensity.comment=Brightness of the light patterns that the caustics cast onto surfaces under water. Higher values make the dancing highlights brighter.
option.rainRipples=Vihmamullid
option.rainRipples.comment=Expanding raindrop ripple rings on still, sky-exposed water. Costs one texture sample per water texel.
option.rainRippleStrength=Vihmamullide Tugevus
option.rainRippleStrength.comment=Adjusts how strongly rain ripples distort the water surface normal. Higher = more pronounced, choppier ripples.
option.snellsWindow=Snelli aken
option.snellsWindow.comment=Täielik sisepeegeldus vee all
option.snellsWindowIntensity=Snell's Window Intensity
option.snellsWindowIntensity.comment=Brightness of Snell's window, the bright circle of sky that is visible from underwater when looking up. Higher values make it more pronounced.
screen.waterAppearance=Välimus
option.waterTexture=Veetekstuur
option.waterTexture.comment=Kuidas kasutada vanilla veetekstuuri.\n\nOff – ei ühtegi tekstuuri.\nHighlights – veetekstuur lisab sära veepinnale, nagu Bedrock RTX‑is.\nVanilla – tekstuur on sama, mis muud tekstuurid
value.waterTexture.waterTextureOff=Väljas
value.waterTexture.waterTextureHighlight=Sära
value.waterTexture.waterTextureVanilla=Vanilla
value.waterTexture.waterTextureHighlightUnderground=Sära (ainult maa all)
option.biomeWaterColor=Biomi-veevärv
option.biomeWaterColor.comment=Vee neeldumine arvestab biomi veevärvi
option.waterTextureIntensity=Water Texture Intensity
option.waterTextureIntensity.comment=Strength of the resource pack's water texture. Higher values make the water texture more visible on the surface.
option.biomeWaterColorIntensity=Biome Water Color Intensity
option.biomeWaterColorIntensity.comment=How strongly the biome's water colour tints the water surface. Higher values make each biome's water more distinct.
option.rainPuddles=Vihmavee lompide efekt
option.rainPuddles.comment=Controls rain puddles on the ground while it's raining.
option.rainPuddlesIntensity=VihmaveeIntensity
option.rainPuddlesIntensity.comment=How strongly rain puddles darken and wet the ground. Higher values make puddles more visible and more reflective.
screen.waterFogCoeff=Veeudu koefitsiendid
screen.waterFogSurface=Vee Kohal
option.waterAbsorptionR=Punase neeldumine
option.waterAbsorptionR.comment=Red component of the water absorption colour. Higher values absorb red light faster, so deep water loses its warmth and turns blue-green.
option.waterAbsorptionG=Rohelise neeldumine
option.waterAbsorptionG.comment=Green component of the water absorption colour. Higher values absorb green light faster.
option.waterAbsorptionB=Sinise neeldumine
option.waterAbsorptionB.comment=Blue component of the water absorption colour. Higher values absorb blue light faster.
option.waterScattering=Hajumine
option.waterScattering.comment=How much light the water scatters back towards the viewer. Higher values make the water look milkier and hide what lies behind it.
screen.waterFogUnderwater=Vee All
option.waterAbsorptionRUnderwater=Punase neeldumine – vee all
option.waterAbsorptionRUnderwater.comment=Red component of the underwater absorption colour. It overrides the surface absorption while you are submerged, so the underwater fog has its own tint.
option.waterAbsorptionGUnderwater=Rohelise neeldumine – vee all
option.waterAbsorptionGUnderwater.comment=Green component of the underwater absorption colour. It overrides the surface absorption while you are submerged.
option.waterAbsorptionBUnderwater=Sinise neeldumine – vee all
option.waterAbsorptionBUnderwater.comment=Blue component of the underwater absorption colour. It overrides the surface absorption while you are submerged.
option.waterScatteringUnderwater=Hajumine – vee all
option.waterScatteringUnderwater.comment=How much light the water scatters back towards the viewer while you are underwater. Higher values make the water look milkier and reduce visibility.
screen.reflections=Peegeldused
option.environmentReflections=Keskkonna peegeldused
option.environmentReflections.comment=Ekraanisisesed peegeldused. Vesi ja läikivad plokid peegeldavad ümbritsevat. Suur jõudluskulu
option.skyReflections=Taeva peegeldused
option.skyReflections.comment=Vesi ja läikivad plokid peegeldavad taevast
option.ssrRoughnessSupport=Kareduse tugi
option.ssrRoughnessSupport.comment=Peegeldused karedate pindade peavad olema kareduse tõttu udused. Suur jõudluskulu
option.ssrRayCount=Kiirte arv
option.ssrRayCount.comment=Kiirte arv karedate pindade peegeldamiseks. Rohkem kiiri = vähem müra, aga halvem jõudlus
option.ssrIntersectionStepsSmooth=Ülemineku sammud – sujuv
option.ssrIntersectionStepsSmooth.comment=Määrab sujuvate peegelduste täpsust jõudluse arvelt
option.ssrIntersectionStepsRough=Ülemineku sammud – kare
option.ssrIntersectionStepsRough.comment=Määrab karedate peegelduste täpsust jõudluse arvelt
option.ssrRefinementSteps=Täpsustussammud
option.ssrRefinementSteps.comment=Reguleerib kõikide peegelduste täpsust jõudluse arvelt
option.ssrRoughnessThresh=Kareduse lävi
option.ssrRoughnessThresh.comment=Määrab, kui sile pind peab olema, et peegeldused ilmuksid
screen.refraction=Murdumine
option.refraction=Murdumine
option.refraction.comment=Selects how the water surface refracts the scene behind it. The different modes trade accuracy for performance.
value.refraction.refractionOff=Väljas
value.refraction.refractionAll=Kõik
value.refraction.refractionWaterOnly=Ainult vesi
option.refractionIntensity=Murdumise intensiivsus
option.refractionIntensity.comment=How strongly the water surface bends what is seen through it. Higher values distort the view behind the water more.
option.dispersionIntensity=Dispersion Intensity
option.dispersionIntensity.comment=Adds chromatic dispersion (RGB fringing) to refracted water/glass, like light splitting through a prism
screen.camera=Camera
option.camSensorWidth=Sensor Width
option.camSensorWidth.comment=Camera sensor width in millimetres. Larger sensors give shallower depth of field at the same aperture.
option.camFstops=Aperture F-Stops
option.camFstops.comment=Lens aperture. Low values (f/0.8) give razor-thin focus; high values (f/16) keep the scene sharp deep into the distance.
option.camShutterSpeed=Shutter Speed
option.camShutterSpeed.comment=Camera shutter speed as 1/N seconds. Slower speeds streak motion blur longer; 1/60 matches the old neutral look.
option.camIso=ISO Sensitivity
option.camIso.comment=Sensor sensitivity. Doubling ISO doubles exposure brightness across manual and auto exposure alike.
screen.dof=Depth of Field
option.dof=Teravussügavus (Depth of Field)
option.dof.comment=Kaamerafookuse efekt – hägustab fookusest väljas olevad alad
option.chromaticDispersion=Chromatic Dispersion
option.chromaticDispersion.comment=Radial spectral fringing scaled by defocus, simulating real camera lens dispersion. In-focus regions stay clean; blurred areas fringe with color.
option.chromaticDispersionStrength=Dispersion Strength
option.chromaticDispersionStrength.comment=Adjusts the strength of the chromatic dispersion fringing. Higher values widen the red/blue separation in out-of-focus areas.
option.dofSamples=Teravussügavuse proovid
option.dofSamples.comment=Proovide arv teravussügavuse jaoks. Rohkem proove = kvaliteetsem hägusus, aga suurem jõudluskulu
option.dofFocus=Teravussügavuse fookus
option.dofFocus.comment=Teravussügavuse fookuskaugus
value.dofFocus.-1.0=Automaatne
option.dofMaxRadius=DoF Max Radius
option.dofMaxRadius.comment=Caps the circle of confusion as a fraction of screen height. Lower values keep backgrounds sharper and save performance; higher values allow creamier blur.
screen.motionBlur=Motion Blur
option.motionBlur=Liikumishägusus
option.motionBlur.comment=Kinolik hägusus liikumisel. Võib aidata sujuvust madalal FPS‑il, aga võib tekitada liikumishaigust
option.motionBlurSamples=Motion Blur Samples
option.motionBlurSamples.comment=Number of samples along the motion trail. Higher values give smoother streaks at higher GPU cost.
option.motionBlurScale=Motion Blur Scale
option.motionBlurScale.comment=Artistic multiplier on the shutter-driven trail length. Shutter speed sets the physical baseline; this scales it.
screen.exposure=Valgustus
option.autoExposure=Automaatne säritus
option.autoExposure.comment=Enables advanced global auto exposure. Automatically adjusts exposure based on scene brightness.
option.localExposure=Local Exposure
option.localExposure.comment=Applies spatially adaptive HDR exposure while preserving the global exposure and protecting highlight and shadow detail.
option.autoExposureMin=Minimaalne säritus
option.autoExposureMin.comment=Lowest exposure the auto exposure may reach. It stops the image from becoming too bright in a very bright scene.
option.autoExposureMax=Maksimaalne säritus
option.autoExposureMax.comment=Highest exposure the auto exposure may reach. It stops the image from becoming too dark in a very dark scene.
option.autoExposureRateDimToBright=Adaptation Speed — Brightening
option.autoExposureRateDimToBright.comment=Adjusts how quickly exposure adapts when the scene gets brighter (e.g., looking from a cave to the sky). Higher = faster adaptation.
option.autoExposureRateBrightToDim=Adaptation Speed — Darkening
option.autoExposureRateBrightToDim.comment=Adjusts how quickly exposure adapts when the scene gets darker (e.g., entering a cave). Higher = faster dimming.
option.manualExposureValue=Käsitsi särituse väärtus
option.manualExposureValue.comment=Fixed exposure value used while the auto exposure is off. Higher values make the image brighter.
option.manualExposureUseScreenBrightness=Kasuta heledusliugurit
option.manualExposureUseScreenBrightness.comment=Särituse väärtus interpoleerib minimaalsete ja maksimaalsete väärtuste vahel Video Seadete heledusliuguri põhjal
option.histogramTarget=Histogrammi sihtväärtus (CDF)
option.histogramTarget.comment=Brightness the histogram exposure aims for, as a percentage of the range. Lower values make the image darker.
option.histogramBins=Histogrammi vahemikud
option.histogramBins.comment=Number of bins the brightness histogram is split into. More bins give a more precise average, but the exposure can also react more slowly.
option.camExposureCompensation=Exposure Compensation
option.camExposureCompensation.comment=EV compensation dial for the exposure triangle. Brightens or darkens around the aperture/shutter/ISO result, like aperture-priority mode on a real camera.
option.histogramShadowWeight=Meter Shadow Weight
option.histogramShadowWeight.comment=Weight of the shadow population in the three-population exposure meter. Higher values protect shadow detail from crushing.
option.histogramHighlightWeight=Meter Highlight Weight
option.histogramHighlightWeight.comment=Weight of the highlight population in the exposure meter. Higher values protect bright areas like sunsets from blowing out.
option.localExposureRegional=Local Regional Blend
option.localExposureRegional.comment=Blends the fine bilateral correction toward area-scale dodge and burn. Higher values adapt whole regions; 0 keeps pixel-local detail only.
option.localExposureRange=Local Regional Range
option.localExposureRange.comment=Maximum exposure shift in stops the regional adaptation may apply. Caps grading so it never overrides global exposure.
option.localExposureDetail=Local Detail Strength
option.localExposureDetail.comment=Scales the fine bilateral detail correction. Lower values leave only the area-scale regional grading.
screen.vignette=Vignette
option.vignette=Vinjett
option.vignette.comment=Tumendab ekraani servi
option.vignetteIntensity=Vinjeti intensiivsus
option.vignetteIntensity.comment=Reguleerib vinjeti tugevust
option.vignetteStart=Vignette Start
option.vignetteStart.comment=Radial distance from screen center where the vignette falloff begins.
option.vignetteEnd=Vignette End
option.vignetteEnd.comment=Radial distance where the vignette reaches full strength.
option.vignetteExponent=Vignette Rolloff
option.vignetteExponent.comment=Shapes the vignette falloff curve. Higher values concentrate darkening toward the corners.
screen.lensFlare=Lens Flare
option.lensFlare=Lens Flare
option.lensFlare.comment=Ghosts, halo and anamorphic streak from bright lights scattering inside the lens. Computed pre-tonemap so flare grades with the scene.
option.lensFlareHalo=Flare Halo
option.lensFlareHalo.comment=Halo ring around the sun on top of the ghost chain.
option.lensFlareIntensity=Flare Intensity
option.lensFlareIntensity.comment=Overall strength of ghosts, halo and streak.
option.lensFlareThresh=Flare Threshold
option.lensFlareThresh.comment=Scene luminance above which highlights seed flare. Lower values let lamps and glints flare; higher isolates the sun.
option.lensFlareGhosts=Ghost Count
option.lensFlareGhosts.comment=Number of ghosts strung along the sun axis. More ghosts cost performance.
option.lensFlareSpacing=Ghost Spacing
option.lensFlareSpacing.comment=Spacing of the ghost chain along the sun-to-center axis.
option.lensFlareHaloRadius=Halo Radius
option.lensFlareHaloRadius.comment=Radius of the halo ring around the sun.
option.lensFlareHaloWidth=Halo Width
option.lensFlareHaloWidth.comment=Width of the soft halo ring drawn around the sun. Higher values make the halo thicker and softer.
screen.bloom=Bloom
option.bloom=Hägusus (Bloom)
option.bloom.comment=Pehme “kumav” efekt heledate alade ja valgusallikate ümber
option.bloomIntensity=Hägususe intensiivsus
option.bloomIntensity.comment=Reguleerib, kui tugevalt hägusus pilti mõjutab
option.bloomUpsamplingFilter=Bloom Filter
option.bloomUpsamplingFilter.comment=Selects the filter used to upsample the bloom buffers. Bilinear is cheap and soft, bicubic keeps the glow sharper but costs a little more.
value.bloomUpsamplingFilter.texture=Bilinear
value.bloomUpsamplingFilter.bicubicFilter=Bicubic
option.bloomSpread=Bloom Spread
option.bloomSpread.comment=Controls the size of the bloom blur. Higher values spread the glow over a larger area.
screen.post=Järeltöötlus
option.displayGamut=Display Gamut
option.displayGamut.comment=Native working/output gamut (needs Iris 1.6.4+ color correction). Keep the Iris client space on sRGB; fog, light and sky follow this setting.
value.displayGamut.displayGamutSrgb=sRGB
value.displayGamut.displayGamutDciP3=DCI-P3
value.displayGamut.displayGamutDisplayP3=Display P3
value.displayGamut.displayGamutRec2020=Rec.2020
value.displayGamut.displayGamutAdobeRgb=Adobe RGB
screen.colorGrading=Värvikorrektsioon
option.tonemap=Toonikaart (Tonemap operaator)
option.tonemap.comment=Selects the tonemapping operator. Tonemapping compresses the very bright values of the scene into the range a display can show, and every operator has its own highlight roll-off and colour response.
value.tonemap.tonemapAcesFit=ACES Fit
value.tonemap.tonemapAcesFull=ACES Full
value.tonemap.tonemapHejl2015=Hejl 2015
value.tonemap.tonemapHejlBurgess=Hejl-Burgess
value.tonemap.tonemapLottes=Lottes
value.tonemap.tonemapUncharted2=Uncharted 2
value.tonemap.tonemapTech=Tech
value.tonemap.tonemapOzius=Ozius
value.tonemap.tonemapReinhard=Reinhard
value.tonemap.tonemapReinhardJodie=Reinhard-Jodie
option.colorGrading=Color Grading
option.colorGrading.comment=Full color grading pipeline: brightness, contrast, white balance, ASC CDL, Oklab contrast, selective hues and tints. Off passes tonemapper output through.
screen.gradingBasic=Põhiseaded
option.gradeBrightness=Heledus
option.gradeBrightness.comment=Overall brightness of the graded image. Higher values brighten the picture, lower values darken it.
option.gradeContrast=Kontrast
option.gradeContrast.comment=Contrast of the graded image. Higher values push the highlights and shadows further apart, lower values flatten the image.
option.gradePivot=Contrast Pivot
option.gradePivot.comment=Luminance anchor for contrast (0–1 linear). 0.18 is photographic middle grey.
option.gradeSaturation=Küllastus
option.gradeSaturation.comment=Saturation of the graded image. Higher values give more vivid colours, lower values give more muted ones.
option.gradeVibrance=Vibrance
option.gradeVibrance.comment=Gentle saturation for muted colors only. Lifts dull areas without oversaturating vivid ones; negatives mute vivid areas.
option.gradeWhiteBalance=Valgebalanss
option.gradeWhiteBalance.comment=Shifts the colour temperature of the graded image. Higher values make the image warmer, lower values make it cooler.
suffix.gradeWhiteBalance=K
screen.gradingWheels=Varjud · Keskt. · Valgused
option.gradeLiftR=§c▍ §fShadow Lift — Red
option.gradeLiftR.comment=Raises or lowers the red channel in the darkest parts of the image (shadows/blacks). Positive = warm shadows, negative = cool shadows.
option.gradeLiftG=§a▍ §fShadow Lift — Green
option.gradeLiftG.comment=Raises or lowers the green channel in shadows. Combine with red and blue lift to tint the darkest tones any color.
option.gradeLiftB=§9▍ §fShadow Lift — Blue
option.gradeLiftB.comment=Raises or lowers the blue channel in shadows. Positive = blue-tinted blacks, negative = yellow-tinted blacks.
option.gradeGammaR=§c▍ §fMidtone Gamma — Red
option.gradeGammaR.comment=Power-curve adjustment for the red channel in midtones. Above 1.0 brightens reds in the middle range; below 1.0 darkens them.
option.gradeGammaG=§a▍ §fMidtone Gamma — Green
option.gradeGammaG.comment=Power-curve adjustment for the green channel in midtones. Useful for shifting the overall midtone hue toward magenta or green.
option.gradeGammaB=§9▍ §fMidtone Gamma — Blue
option.gradeGammaB.comment=Power-curve adjustment for the blue channel in midtones. Above 1.0 adds a cool blue cast to midtones.
option.gradeGainR=§c▍ §fHighlight Gain — Red
option.gradeGainR.comment=Multiplies the red channel in the brightest parts of the image. Above 1.0 warms highlights; below 1.0 cools them.
option.gradeGainG=§a▍ §fHighlight Gain — Green
option.gradeGainG.comment=Multiplies the green channel in highlights. Combine with red and blue gain to tint the brightest tones.
option.gradeGainB=§9▍ §fHighlight Gain — Blue
option.gradeGainB.comment=Multiplies the blue channel in highlights. Positive = cool blue highlights, negative = warm yellow highlights.
screen.gradingCurve=Tooni Kõver
option.gradeOklabPivot=Perceptual Contrast Pivot
option.gradeOklabPivot.comment=The lightness value in Oklab space (0–1) that stays fixed when the perceptual contrast slider is applied. 0.5 = perceptual midpoint.
option.gradeOklabContrast=Perceptual Contrast
option.gradeOklabContrast.comment=Perceptual contrast in Oklab space. Preserves hue in saturated areas, unlike linear contrast.
option.gradeBlackPoint=Black Point
option.gradeBlackPoint.comment=Raises the minimum output level, lifting blacks toward grey. Useful for a faded/matte look or to match a display with elevated black levels. 0 = true black.
option.gradeWhitePoint=White Point
option.gradeWhitePoint.comment=Lowers the maximum output level, compressing highlights toward grey. Useful for a filmic, low-contrast look. 0 = full white.
screen.gradingSplitTone=Jagatud Tonaalsus
option.gradeShadowLow=Shadow Range — Low
option.gradeShadowLow.comment=The lower luminance boundary of the shadow tonal range used by the three-way color wheel. Pixels below this value are fully in the shadow zone.
option.gradeShadowHigh=Shadow Range — High
option.gradeShadowHigh.comment=The upper luminance boundary of the shadow zone. Pixels between Shadow Low and Shadow High blend between shadow and midtone color wheels.
option.gradeHighlightLow=Highlight Range — Low
option.gradeHighlightLow.comment=The lower luminance boundary of the highlight zone. Pixels between Highlight Low and Highlight High blend between midtone and highlight color wheels.
option.gradeHighlightHigh=Highlight Range — High
option.gradeHighlightHigh.comment=The upper luminance boundary of the highlight zone. Pixels above this value are fully in the highlight zone.
option.gradeShadowStrength=Shadow Tint Strength
option.gradeShadowStrength.comment=How strongly the shadow color wheel hue is applied to dark areas. 0 = no tint, 1 = full tint at the chosen shadow hue and saturation.
option.gradeShadowHue=Shadow Hue
option.gradeShadowHue.comment=The hue angle (0–360°) of the color tint applied to shadows when Shadow Tint Strength > 0. 220° = cool blue-purple, 30° = warm orange.
option.gradeMidStrength=Midtone Tint Strength
option.gradeMidStrength.comment=How strongly the midtone color wheel hue is applied to middle-luminance areas.
option.gradeMidHue=Midtone Hue
option.gradeMidHue.comment=The hue angle of the color tint applied to midtones when Midtone Tint Strength > 0.
option.gradeHighlightStrength=Highlight Tint Strength
option.gradeHighlightStrength.comment=How strongly the highlight color wheel hue is applied to bright areas.
option.gradeHighlightHue=Highlight Hue
option.gradeHighlightHue.comment=The hue angle of the color tint applied to highlights when Highlight Tint Strength > 0. 45° = warm golden highlights.
option.gradeShadowTintSat=Shadow Tint Saturation
option.gradeShadowTintSat.comment=Saturation of the dedicated shadow tint. 0 = no tint, 1 = fully saturated shadow cast at the chosen hue.
option.gradeShadowTintHue=Shadow Tint Hue
option.gradeShadowTintHue.comment=Hue angle for the dedicated shadow tint pass (separate from the three-way wheel). Lets you add a subtle color cast to just the darkest tones.
option.gradeHighlightTintSat=Highlight Tint Saturation
option.gradeHighlightTintSat.comment=Saturation of the dedicated highlight tint. 0 = no tint, 1 = fully saturated highlight cast.
option.gradeHighlightTintHue=Highlight Tint Hue
option.gradeHighlightTintHue.comment=Hue angle for the dedicated highlight tint pass. Adds a color cast to only the brightest parts of the image.
screen.gradingSelective=Valikuline Värv
option.gradeOrangeSatBoost=Oranži küllastus
option.gradeOrangeSatBoost.comment=Extra saturation applied to orange tones only. It keeps skin and warm lights vivid without oversaturating the whole image.
option.gradeTealSatBoost=Türkiissinine küllastus
option.gradeTealSatBoost.comment=Extra saturation applied to teal tones only. It keeps shadows and cool water vivid without oversaturating the whole image.
option.gradeGreenSatBoost=Roheline küllastus
option.gradeGreenSatBoost.comment=Extra saturation applied to green tones only. It keeps foliage vivid without oversaturating the whole image.
option.gradeGreenHueShift=Roheline tooninihe
option.gradeGreenHueShift.comment=Shifts the hue of green tones. Use it to push foliage towards yellow green or towards blue green.
suffix.gradeGreenHueShift=°
option.gradeSelectiveBlend=Selective Grade Blend
option.gradeSelectiveBlend.comment=Master blend weight for all selective color adjustments (orange/teal/green saturation and green hue shift). 0 = no selective grading, 1 = full effect.
screen.academyColor=Academy Color (ACES)
option.academyRrtExposure=ACES RRT Exposure
option.academyRrtExposure.comment=Exposure in stops before the RRT. Moves the scene along the filmic S-curve itself.
option.academyRrtGamma=ACES RRT Gamma
option.academyRrtGamma.comment=Gamma shaping applied inside the RRT before the tonescale. Above 1.0 darkens midtones into the curve, below 1.0 lifts them.
option.academyRrtGlow=ACES RRT Glow
option.academyRrtGlow.comment=RRT glow lifting dim saturated colors. Higher means dreamier highlights; 0.10 is default.
option.academyRrtSat=ACES RRT Saturation
option.academyRrtSat.comment=Global desaturation inside the RRT sweeteners. Lower = more filmic muted response before the tonescale. 0.96 matches the reference fit.
option.academyOdtSat=ACES ODT Saturation
option.academyOdtSat.comment=Desaturation in the output device transform compensating luminance differences. Lower tames oversaturated brights after the tonescale.
screen.aa=Anti-Aliasing
option.taau=TAA skaleerimine (Upscaling)
option.taau.comment=Renderdab stseenivärvid väiksemas lahutuses ja suurendab need TAA abil. Suurendab jõudlust, kuid võib vähendada kvaliteeti ja lisada artefakte
option.fxaa=FXAA
option.fxaa.comment=Silub ääri. Töötab koos TAA‑ga, eriti liikumise ajal. Väga kasulik koos TAAU‑ga
option.cas=Kujutise teravustamine
option.cas.comment=Teravustab lõpppilti (kontrastipõhine teravustamine)
option.taauRenderScale=TAAU renderduse skaala
option.taauRenderScale.comment=Skaala, mille järgi stseenivärv renderdatakse, kui TAAU on lubatud. Näiteks kui resolutsioon on 1920x1080 ja skaala on 0.75, renderdatakse see 1440x810
option.fxaaIntensity=FXAA Strength
option.fxaaIntensity.comment=Adjusts the strength of fast approximate anti-aliasing. Higher = smoother edges but softer image.
screen.purkinjeShiftTransform=Purkinje nihke
option.purkinjeShift=Purkinje nihkumine
option.purkinjeShift.comment=Simuleerib inimese nägemise muutumist hämaras valguses: värvide kahvatus ja punaste toonide tumenemine
option.purkinjeShiftR=§c▍ §fPurkinje Response — Red
option.purkinjeShiftR.comment=Red channel weight of the scotopic tint. Lower values push night vision cooler.
option.purkinjeShiftG=§a▍ §fPurkinje Response — Green
option.purkinjeShiftG.comment=Green channel weight of the scotopic tint. Rods peak in blue-green, so this dominates the night hue.
option.purkinjeShiftB=§9▍ §fPurkinje Response — Blue
option.purkinjeShiftB.comment=Blue channel weight of the scotopic tint. Higher values deepen the classic blue night shift.
option.purkinjeShiftIntensity=Purkinje nihke tugevus
option.purkinjeShiftIntensity.comment=How strongly the Purkinje effect is applied. Higher values desaturate the image more and tint it deep red, the way the eye sees in near darkness.
screen.framingTool=Framing Tool
option.framingTool=Framing Tool
option.framingTool.comment=Master toggle for composition guides (rule-of-thirds, aspect box, safe area). For lining up screenshots.
option.framingThirds=Thirds Grid
option.framingThirds.comment=Overlays a rule-of-thirds grid on the screen so you can line up shots against the thirds.
option.framingAspect=Aspect Guides
option.framingAspect.comment=Target aspect-ratio box and safe-area guides. It frames the screen so you can check how the shot will be cropped.
option.framingOpacity=Guide Opacity
option.framingOpacity.comment=Opacity of the framing guides. Higher values make the guides easier to see against the scene.
option.framingLineWidth=Line Width
option.framingLineWidth.comment=Thickness in pixels of the framing guides. Higher values draw thicker lines.
option.framingAspectRatio=Aspect Ratio
option.framingAspectRatio.comment=Target aspect ratio (width over height) for the crop box.
option.framingSafeArea=Safe Area
option.framingSafeArea.comment=Centered safe-area fraction shown inside the aspect box.
